  "interoperability.metadata.txt": "@prefix schema:  <https://schema.org/> .\n@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .\n\n<https://example.org/ko/example/1.0>\n    a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;\n\n    # 1. Semantics\n    schema:about\n        <https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/semantics> ;\n\n    # 2. Data object profiles\n    dcterms:conformsTo\n        <https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/profiles> ;\n\n    # 3. Interface\n    schema:potentialAction\n        <https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/interface> ;\n\n    # Identity and version\n    schema:identifier\n        \"example-ko\" ;\n\n    schema:version\n        \"1.0\" .\n\n\n<https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/semantics>\n    schema:object\n        <https://example.org/concept/InputConcept> ;\n\n    schema:result\n        <https://example.org/concept/OutputConcept> .\n\n\n<https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/profiles>\n    schema:object\n        <https://example.org/profile/InputProfile/1.0> ;\n\n    schema:result\n        <https://example.org/profile/OutputProfile/1.0> .\n\n\n<https://example.org/ko/example/1.0/interface>\n    schema:target\n        <urn:javascript:function:run> .\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# Minimal Interoperability Profile\n#\n# schema:about points to the input and output semantics.\n#\n# dcterms:conformsTo points to the accepted input and\n# produced output data object profiles.\n#\n# schema:potentialAction points to the JavaScript interface.\n#\n# schema:object denotes an input.\n# schema:result denotes an output.\n#\n# urn:javascript:function:run denotes the exercise convention:\n# knowledgeObject.run(input).\n#\n# These are profile conventions for this metadata pattern.\n# They do not redefine the source vocabularies.\n# ============================================================\n```",
